  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to local conflict resolution mechanisms, delivery of justice and protection of the poor and the vulnerable people ensured.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">The population in East Darfur have long been suffering impacts of low and high profile conflicts which impaired its ability to develop solutions that help it recover from shocks and devastating effects caused by conflict and other disasters.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Continuation of above 2021-2022 Targets:</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2: Ensure peace dividends for community interdependence and co-existence are delivered through diverse livelihoods options and effective natural resource management:

2. Income Generating Activities (IGAs):
- 35 (1 women, 34 men): 35 youth (34 male and 1 female from Um Gutna, 5 youth from each community) provided with small grants to start their small businesses. Each youth was given 190,200 SDGs to start their small business (25 chose agriculture project, 7 chose animal fattening goats and 3 chose phone charging using solar energy.)</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">2021-2022 Targets:

Output 1: Community-based conflict resolution and reconciliation mechanisms are in use and working effectively to resolve conflict.
&#x2022; Organize 7 community consultations for CBRMs formation
&#x2022; Develop the CBRM ToR for 7 communities
&#x2022; Selection of 50%-women community committees
&#x2022; Orientation of CBRM
&#x2022; Train CBRM in conflict analysis and resolution
&#x2022; Train CBRMs in conflict and GBV case management 
&#x2022; Provision of operating material for CBRM

Output 2: Peace dividends for community interdependence and co-existence delivered
&#x2022; Rehabilitation of 1 water yard
&#x2022; Formation of 1 water management committees 
&#x2022; Train 1 community water management committees
&#x2022; Demarcation of migration routes - 20km
&#x2022; Construction of 20 kilometers of fire lines
&#x2022; Capacity building of 7 range management committees 
&#x2022; Train 7 communities (10 from each community) in negotiation and maintenance of peaceful coexistence
&#x2022; Establish and construct 7 community centers by local materials
&#x2022; Building women capacity for effective political participation
&#x2022; Provision of small grants to 35 youth 
&#x2022; Distribution of 175 goats to 35 families
&#x2022; Refresher training to 21 para-vets
&#x2022; Organization of one day of business training to 35 community members
&#x2022; Increase community awareness and knowledge about gender and gender transformation
&#x2022; Awareness raising and protection of women, men, and children GBV and its impact
&#x2022; Carry out literacy and numeracy education for women and children out of schools 
&#x2022; Community awareness-raising and knowledge improvement about Covid-19 management
&#x2022; Carry out 2 vaccination campaigns to vaccinate 100000 heads of livestock

Output 3: Women&#xb4;s organizations, including those representing pastoralist women, empowered to meaningfully participate in local and State-level peacebuilding platforms.
&#x2022; Identify women organizations and train their membership
&#x2022; Form and establish womens organizations
&#x2022; Raise womens capacity to participate in the political arena
&#x2022; Organize nomadic women in community-based organizations
&#x2022; Train womens organizations in dialogue, conflict, and political analysis

Output 4: Improved networking, coordination, and learning between local and state-level peacebuilding institutions
&#x2022; Revive peacebuilding institutions
&#x2022; Establish and organize nomadic womens economic groups and CBOs
&#x2022; Conduct cross-project village exchange visits</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022; 7 committees formed in each of the project implementation villages (105 members).
&#x2022; 3 Community Centers constructed in Um Eid, Azumri, and Al Ardeib. The centres will become the gathering place for the community where they can discuss and manage community issues particularly the youth. The centres are also places where the community women organizations can meet and plan for their initiatives.
&#x2022; Demarcation of 20km migration routes and one day business training to 35 community members to be carried out in next quarter. 
&#x2022; 7 Women organization identified. The organizations have been established in communities where no form of organization brings women together over certain objectives. The newly established women organizations, after being trained and incapacitated, will lead their own social, economic, or political initiatives.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
